        "title": "Microsoft CEO says Xbox streamlining is \"great to see\"",
        "description": "Satya Nadella said he feels \"fantastic\" about Xbox’s remaining studios and intellectual‑property portfolio during a discussion on the Sources Podca...",
        "fullContent": "Satya Nadella said he feels \"fantastic\" about Xbox’s remaining studios and intellectual‑property portfolio during a discussion on the Sources Podcast, noting the recent restructuring of the business. He described the ongoing \"streamlining\" efforts as \"great to see\".\n\nNadella added that the newly appointed Xbox chief executive, Asha Sharma, is tasked with returning the gaming division to growth by concentrating on the company’s biggest titles and exploring new business models. He said the goal is to develop a sustainable model that can deliver games to a larger audience and to serve as both a publisher and a platform provider for PC and Xbox."
      },
